Theorem VF-6: contracts and realization agreement — composes VF-3 oracle + VF-4 FIP balance

  Preconditions:
    - VF-6 governs the contracts-realization agreement invariant per Annex E §AIMS VF-6: "Contracts and realization SHALL agree. MemoryContract says
      FipContract::Certified -> realized IR has zero unmatched alloc/dealloc."
      Restated by Annex E §AIMS §2 invariant 1: "Contracts and realization
      must agree."
    - VF-6's concrete shape is MemoryContract x ArcFunction -> Bool per
      aims-proof/proofs/01-verification/Verification.proof: analysis inferences
      match realized behavior. The realized-side check is what the VF-3 oracle
      performs; VF-6 is the AGREEMENT invariant the verification stack as a whole
      enforces. Discharged here against the sec-01 Verification.proof sorry
      obligation.
    - VF-6 COMPOSES VF-3 (the realized-side oracle re-derivation refinement) and
      VF-4 (the FIP alloc-balance) into a single contract-realization
      implication: a Certified claim requires BOTH the realized IR alloc-balanced
      (VF-4) AND the oracle re-derivation refining the inferred contract (VF-3).
    - TARGET-ONLY whole-stack mandate: there is no single shipped verifier
      function — VF-6 is the agreement invariant the layered stack asserts
      (composing the shipped VF-3 oracle.rs and VF-4 fip.rs verifiers).
      conformance: target-only.
    - depends-on sec-06: IC-3 + IC-5 + IC-6 contract soundness is load-bearing
      for the contract side of the agreement.

  Soundness property:
    Forall inferred MemoryContract C and realized ArcFunction F:

      (P1) Certified implies balanced-and-refined: when C claims
           FipContract::Certified, C and F are in AGREEMENT iff F's realized IR
           is alloc-balanced (the VF-4 verdict) AND the oracle re-derivation of
           F refines C (the VF-3 verdict). Both sub-checks must hold.

      (P2) Disagreement is an error: a Certified contract over an unbalanced
           realized IR (VF-4 fails), or a contract the oracle cannot refine
           (VF-3 fails), is a violation. A non-Certified contract still requires
           oracle refinement (VF-3 applies regardless of the Certified claim);
           the FIP balance is asserted only when Certified is claimed.

    VF-6 is the agreement capstone of the verification stack: it ties the
    contract claim to the realized behavior. A contract that claims FIP while
    the realized IR leaks, or a contract whose inferred dimensions the oracle
    re-derivation contradicts, breaks the through-line from proof to
    realization.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the refinement engine via composition of the VF-3
    oracle refinement and the VF-4 FIP balance into the agreement implication
    (per the proof-checker design sec-Engine-per-Category-Inventory VF row; the foundational-axiom policy
    sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape — definitional rewriting +
    constructive ->-introduction).

    Part (P1/P2) — agreement grid:

      The verifier models the agreement predicate (Certified -> balanced AND
      oracle-refines; non-Certified -> oracle-refines) and asserts it over a
      grid:
        certified_balanced_refines_agree — Certified + balanced + refines
                                              -> agreement.
        certified_unbalanced_disagree — Certified + unbalanced
                                              -> disagreement (VF-4 fails).
        certified_oracle_unsafe_disagree — Certified + balanced + oracle
                                              cannot refine -> disagreement (VF-3).
        noncertified_refines_agree — non-Certified + refines
                                              -> agreement (FIP not asserted).
        noncertified_oracle_unsafe_disagree — non-Certified + oracle cannot
                                              refine -> disagreement (VF-3 still
                                              applies).
      Coverage gate: 5 rows (2 agree + 3 disagree).

    Negative-direction witness (the agreement has teeth — a Certified-over-
    unbalanced contract is REJECTED):
      A Certified contract over an unbalanced realized IR is NOT in agreement;
      accepting it would let the contract claim FIP while the realized IR leaks.

    Engines dispatched:
      refinement (PRIMARY — section_09::verify_vf6_contracts_realization_agreement;
        agreement implication composing VF-3 oracle refinement + VF-4 FIP
        balance; emits Fail on an agreement/disagreement mismatch)
      structural_induction (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the
        coverage-manifest VF row)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      interprocedural_summary (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_09 refinement engine discharges VF-6 via the contract-realization agreement implication composing VF-3 oracle refinement and VF-4 FIP balance (Certified implies alloc-balanced AND oracle-refines; non-Certified implies oracle-refines): 5 rows (2 agree + 3 disagree across VF-3/VF-4 failure modes) with a negative-direction witness rejecting a Certified contract over an unbalanced realized IR; VF-6 is a target-only whole-stack agreement mandate
